    "note": "the chassis: a plate with a hip pin at each corner, and on the front of it a neck, a head with a muzzle and ears, and at the back a tail. The pins are what the legs mate to, so their diameter is the one number the legs have to agree with; everything forward of the neck is silhouette, and silhouette is what makes it read as a dog rather than as a table"
